diff --git a/sway/sway-output.5.scd b/sway/sway-output.5.scd
--- a/sway/sway-output.5.scd
+++ b/sway/sway-output.5.scd
@@ -210,6 +210,22 @@ must be separated by one space. For example:
 
 	This setting only has effect when a window is fullscreen on the output.
 
+*output* <name> zoom <factor>|off
+	Enlarges everything shown on the output by _factor_, a decimal number
+	from 1 to 32. A factor of 1, or _off_, disables the enlargement, which
+	is the default.
+
+	The output then shows a rectangle of the layout that is _factor_ times
+	smaller than the output, including windows, layer surfaces and the
+	pointer. Windows, outputs and input coordinates are not changed, so
+	clients are not told about the enlargement. The shown rectangle follows
+	the pointer and the keyboard focus, see *zoom_mouse_tracking* and
+	*zoom_focus_tracking* in *sway*(5). The _zoom_ command in *sway*(5)
+	changes the factor of the output under the pointer.
+
+	Like other output settings, the factor is kept when the output is
+	disabled or disconnected.
+
 # SEE ALSO
 
 *sway*(5) *sway-input*(5)
diff --git a/sway/sway.5.scd b/sway/sway.5.scd
--- a/sway/sway.5.scd
+++ b/sway/sway.5.scd
@@ -975,6 +975,50 @@ The default colors are:
 	switch to workspace 2, then invoke the *workspace 2* command again, you
 	will be returned to workspace 1. Default is _no_.
 
+*zoom* in [<step>]
+	Raises the enlargement factor of the output under the pointer by _step_,
+	a positive decimal number. The default step is 1. The factor does not go
+	above 32.
+
+*zoom* out [<step>]
+	Lowers the enlargement factor of the output under the pointer by _step_,
+	a positive decimal number. The default step is 1. The factor does not go
+	below 1.
+
+*zoom* set <factor>
+	Sets the enlargement factor of the output under the pointer, a decimal
+	number from 1 to 32. A factor of 1, or _off_, disables the enlargement.
+
+*zoom* off
+	Disables the enlargement of the output under the pointer.
+
+*zoom* toggle
+	Toggles the enlargement of the output under the pointer. Toggling an
+	enlarged output disables the enlargement; toggling an output that is not
+	enlarged restores the most recent factor above 1 it used, or 2.
+
+	Each _zoom_ command works like setting the factor of the output under
+	the pointer with *output* <name> zoom <factor> (see *sway-output*(5)).
+	An enlarged output shows a part of the layout, its _view_, enlarged to
+	fill the output, while windows, input and outputs keep their geometry.
+
+*zoom_focus_tracking* centered|push|none
+	Sets how the view of an enlarged output follows the keyboard focus when
+	a window is focused other than through the pointer, for example by a
+	command, a key binding, a workspace switch or a new window. Only the
+	output of the focused window moves its view. _centered_ centers the view
+	on the window. _push_ moves the view by the smallest amount that shows
+	the whole window, or shows its top-left corner when the window is bigger
+	than the view. _none_ leaves the view alone. Default is _none_.
+
+*zoom_mouse_tracking* centered|proportional|push|none
+	Sets how the view of an enlarged output follows the pointer when it moves
+	over that output. _proportional_ keeps the pointer at the same relative
+	position in the view as on the output. _centered_ keeps the pointer in
+	the middle of the view, except near the edges of the output. _push_ only
+	moves the view by the smallest amount that keeps the pointer inside it.
+	_none_ leaves the view alone. Default is _proportional_.
+
 # CRITERIA
 
